# PR workflow

Details: `.cursor/skills/pr-workflow/SKILL.md`. Graph: `docs/agent-graph-pr.md`.

## Hard gates

1. **Every update gets a PR** — Open an open (non-draft) PR for every code, docs, or agent-rules change; push follow-ups to that same branch.
2. **UI changes → screenshots in the PR body** before `[ready]`.
3. **Babysit → `[ready]` only when green** — All required checks pass and actionable review comments resolved. On every new push, **strip** `[ready]` first; re-add only when green again. Do not merge until Tam explicitly asks.

## Creating PRs

- Always create as open (ready for review) — never draft unless Tam asks.
- Target `main`. Prefer merge commits (no squash) unless Tam says otherwise.
- Conventional commits; keep PR commits related to the change only.
- Optional worktrees under `../kids-worktrees/pr-<N>`.

## Checklist

1. Implement on a feature branch (worktree optional).
2. Commit, push, open non-draft PR to `main`.
3. Fill shared-state block in the PR body (`docs/agent-graph-pr.md`).
4. Run `/verifier` (and `/security-auditor` / `/ui-reviewer` as applicable) in fresh context.
5. Babysit CI + comments; set `[ready]` only when green.
6. Stop — wait for Tam to merge.
7. After merge: cleanup worktree if used. Deploy is TBD until a deploy path exists.

## Must not

- Ship without a PR, or leave the PR as draft (unless asked)
- Mark UI PRs `[ready]` without screenshots
- Mark `[ready]` while checks fail/pending
- Leave `[ready]` after new pushes
- Merge without an explicit Tam ask
- Force-push to `main` or skip hooks
